      "writtenOn": "2018-11-27T20:17:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue happens on POWER_S3. It now moves the power-off process to POWER_S3S5. The POWER_GOOD signal in POWER_S3 may still be high. So we can\u0027t differentiate the transition among S3 -\u003e S3S5, S3 -\u003e S3S0, and S3 -\u003e S3. Introducing this flag can differentiate them:\n * shutdown_from_s0 !\u003d 0: the transition of S3 -\u003e S3S5\n * shutdown_from_s0 \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 AP_SUSPEND_L \u003d\u003d 0: the transition of S3 -\u003e S3 (not there yet)\n * shutdown_from_s0 \u003d\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 AP_SUSPEND_L \u003d\u003d 1: the transition of S3 -\u003e S3S0",
      "parentUuid": "9b98792c_e232787b",
